Qt5 uses the pinned NickelTC image in qt5/Dockerfile. Its upstream recipes,
patches and source references are available at https://github.com/pgaskin/NickelTC.
The exact source revisions of all components in that binary image have not been
verified. The image digest identifies binaries, not a complete source archive.
Debian package notices and package status from NickelTC are retained under
/usr/share/doc/kobuild/nickeltc-packages, nickeltc-common-licenses and
nickeltc-package-status. This metadata covers the upstream image's packages;
it is not an inventory of only the files copied into this SDK.

Qt6 builds the official archive recorded in qt6/source/source.json with the
included patches. The prepared Qt source, patch inputs, license notices and
build scripts are bundled in /usr/src/kobuild/qt6-source.tar.xz. The source
archive includes third-party code bundled in Qt under its original terms.
Qt patch notices are also available at
/usr/share/doc/kobuild/qt6-patches-NOTICE.

Qt license texts are included in /usr/share/doc/kobuild/qt-licenses inside both
images. Ubuntu package notices remain in /usr/share/doc. The Qt6 source archive
does not contain the sources for Ubuntu packages or the cross compiler. This
repository is not a complete corresponding-source archive for the whole image.

Application-specific dependencies and patches are not included.
